\"`) succeed, the Rust implementation reads the full name up to the trailing `$` and trims trailing whitespace.\n\n9. **Public API stubs** — `parse_instruction`, `parse_timestamp`, and `parse_assignment` keep their exported signatures (taking `&File`) but return an \"unsupported\" error since the actual parser uses the in-memory `Reader`. `get_signal_index(&str)` delegates to the byte-based helper."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":206,"cache_read_input_tokens":52974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":206,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b30973aa-5519-4040-a309-76912ddf44e5","uuid":"142527f4-0efb-4524-bcae-63ef369cfa17"}
